#!/usr/bin/python3
"""
loki-nas-maint — restricted maintenance dispatcher for the UGREEN NAS.

Installed root-owned at /usr/local/sbin/loki-nas-maint and reachable only via a
single narrowly scoped sudoers rule. Loki calls it over SSH; it is the ONLY
privileged entry point the NAS exposes to dex247.

Contract:
  - argv is exactly one token, matched against a fixed action table. There is
    no path, container name, image, format string, Docker argument or shell
    fragment a caller can influence. Targets are discovered internally.
  - Two tiers of action. READ-ONLY (ACTIONS): ps, inspect, logs (bounded),
    stats --no-stream, events over a bounded past window. These take no
    arguments at all.
    APPROVAL-GATED WRITES (WRITE_ACTIONS): prepare / backup / apply / verify /
    rollback for the Tracearr update workflow. These additionally use pull,
    exec (pg_dump only) and `compose up -d --no-deps <service>`. There is NO
    rm, rmi, stop, kill, down, prune, volume or network verb anywhere in this
    file, so nothing here can delete or tear down a container, image, volume
    or network.
  - At most ONE caller-supplied value ever crosses the boundary, and only for
    two write actions: a content digest (^sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}$) or a prepare
    id (^[0-9a-f]{16}$). The repository is hardcoded, so an approved digest
    can only be pulled from TRACEARR_REPO. No path, tag, container name or
    Docker argument is ever accepted.
  - apply refuses unless verified backups exist AND the prepare id matches the
    recorded plan AND the running image still matches what was planned, so an
    approval cannot be replayed against different state.
  - Output is JSON on stdout. Environment variable VALUES are never emitted —
    only their names. Labels are allowlisted. Log lines pass a redactor.

Pass 3 additions (network / disk / Plex diagnostics):
  - READ-ONLY (ACTIONS): network_status, network_tooling_check, disk_status,
    plex_status, plex_dependencies, plex_recent_logs, plex_transcode_processes.
    Same contract as the rest of ACTIONS: no arguments, no caller-influenced
    path or command.
  - EPHEMERAL (still zero arguments, still no persisted state):
    network_speed_test starts a ONE-OFF iperf3 server
    (`-1`) wrapped in a fixed `timeout`, bound only to the discovered LAN IP,
    on a fixed port. It always exits — either after serving one client or
    when the timeout fires — so nothing is ever left listening.
  - APPROVAL-GATED WRITE (WRITE_ACTIONS): plex_restart. The ONLY verb it uses
    is `docker start` on a container already confirmed STOPPED — never
    `restart`, `stop`, or `kill`. This mirrors the narrowness of the existing
    Tracearr pull/exec/recreate exception: one new, deterministic, reversible
    action (starting something that is already off), not a general
    stop/kill/restart capability.

Exit codes: 0 ok · 2 unknown/malformed action · 3 discovery failed · 4 docker error
"""

import datetime
import hashlib
import ipaddress
import json
import re
import os
import shutil
import socket
import subprocess
import sys
